# The api image installs its own dependencies and reads TypeScript directly, so
# nothing from the host belongs in the context. `data` matters most: it is the
# local SQLite, and copying it into an image would ship a developer's database
# and then be shadowed by the mounted volume anyway.
node_modules
data
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
npm-debug.log*
